{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2249","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2249","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2249\",\"parent_revision\":\"22a056328a9254dc20543b1f052a922891d4b9c85a45dd530273cf230ad7c8f8\",\"root_revision\":\"22a056328a9254dc20543b1f052a922891d4b9c85a45dd530273cf230ad7c8f8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY (2026-05-22)\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Create a new skill at .claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md that runs 7 parallel git analysis pipelines, cross-references hotspots with bug magnets to produce a high-risk file list, and writes walkthrough/recon-report.md with 8 named sections.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- .claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md exists, passes `uvx skilllint@latest check .claude/skills/git-history-recon/`, and when invoked produces walkthrough/recon-report.md with all 8 required section headers and non-empty High-Risk Files computed as hotspots \u2229 bug-magnets with per-file primary owner annotation.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE with high-confidence basis.\\n\\nConditions verified:\\n1. Frontmatter schema: AVAILABLE \u2014 .claude/rules/frontmatter-requirements.md\\n2. Skill directory placement: AVAILABLE \u2014 .claude/skills/git-history-recon/ (one level deep)\\n3. Output directory convention: AVAILABLE \u2014 walkthrough/ consistent with linear-walkthrough\\n4. All 7 git pipeline commands: AVAILABLE \u2014 exact commands in item \\\"Target state\\\" + research insights file\\n5. Repo-size probe logic: DERIVABLE \u2014 thresholds from Improvement 1 in same research file (small <500 commits, medium 500-10k, large >10k)\\n6. Cross-reference logic: AVAILABLE \u2014 hotspots \u2229 bug-magnets + git shortlog -sn -- <file>\\n7. Report template (8 section headers): AVAILABLE \u2014 exact strings in \\\"Measurable signal\\\"\\n8. Parallel dispatch instruction: AVAILABLE \u2014 \\\"individual Bash calls or single helper script\\\"\\n9. skilllint frontmatter rules: AVAILABLE \u2014 frontmatter-requirements.md\\n10. Citation requirements: AVAILABLE \u2014 source URL https://github.com/yujiachen-y/codebase-recon-skill + research insights file\\n11. linear-walkthrough integration: AVAILABLE \u2014 no modification needed (additive only)\\n12. Markdown formatting rules: AVAILABLE \u2014 CLAUDE.md formatting standards\\n\\nAssumptions to confirm before writing:\\n- Repo-size thresholds (<500 / 500-10k / >10k commits) sourced from Improvement 1 of research/insights/2026-05-10-codebase-recon-skill-improvements.md \u2014 confirmed in current session.\\n\\nImplementation scope:\\n- Single new file: .claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md\\n- No modifications to any existing skill or agent\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **new skill: git-history-recon for codebase risk profiling before code review** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/codebase-recon-skill.md \u2014 pattern: Seven-Dimension Parallel Analysis + Cross-Referencing and Risk Identification\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Addresses a genuine gap: no local skill performs git-history-based risk identification. Code-review agents currently operate without file-level risk signal. Benefit is highest when reviewing large or legacy codebases with concentrated fix-commit history.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Code-review agents (`@dh:code-reviewer`, `.claude/agents/code-review.md`) receive no git-derived signal indicating which files are highest-risk.\\n- Bottleneck: Orchestrator must manually construct git pipelines to produce hotspot + bug-magnet data before each review; the output is lost between sessions because no skill captures or formats it.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Code-review agents can direct attention to the intersection of hotspot files and bug-magnet files \u2014 the highest signal-to-noise risk indicator.\\n- `linear-walkthrough` gains a Phase 1 Discovery artifact to prioritize file coverage.\\n- Onboarding workflows get a machine-readable codebase risk profile.\\n- Risk analysis is repeatable and cached in `walkthrough/recon-report.md` across sessions.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `/git-history-recon` is invoked on a git repository, it runs 7 parallel git analysis pipelines, cross-references hotspots with bug magnets to produce a high-risk file list with primary owner annotations, and writes `walkthrough/recon-report.md` containing 8 named sections. The report is readable by any downstream agent without further git pipeline construction.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable end state:\\n- `.claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md` exists with frontmatter `name: git-history-recon`.\\n- Running `/git-history-recon` on a git repo writes `walkthrough/recon-report.md`.\\n- The report contains exactly these section headers: `## Code Hotspots`, `## Bug Magnets`, `## High-Risk Files`, `## Bus Factor`, `## Team Momentum`, `## Firefighting Frequency`, `## Recently Added Files`, `## Recommendations`.\\n- Each section contains at least one entry sourced from the corresponding git command.\\n- The High-Risk Files section is the set intersection of hotspots and bug magnets, each annotated with its `git shortlog -sn -- <file>` primary owner.\\n- `uvx skilllint@latest check .claude/skills/git-history-recon/` exits 0.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `.claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md` exists and passes `uvx skilllint@latest check .claude/skills/git-history-recon/`.\\n2. `/git-history-recon` invoked on this repository produces `walkthrough/recon-report.md`.\\n3. Report contains all 8 section headers: `## Code Hotspots`, `## Bug Magnets`, `## High-Risk Files`, `## Bus Factor`, `## Team Momentum`, `## Firefighting Frequency`, `## Recently Added Files`, `## Recommendations`.\\n4. High-Risk Files section is non-empty when the repo has any file in both hotspots and bug magnets.\\n5. Each entry in High-Risk Files includes a primary owner from `git shortlog -sn -- <file>`.\\n6. `linear-walkthrough` skill can reference the report as a Phase 1 Discovery artifact without modification to that skill.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/linear-walkthrough/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | .claude/agents/code-review.md |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/create-merge-request-changelog/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | research/insights/2026-05-10-codebase-recon-skill-improvements.md |\\n| External | https://github.com/yujiachen-y/codebase-recon-skill (source pattern)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None (additive skill, no existing consumers require it)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall-Medium \u2014 new skill file only; no Python implementation required. Git commands are fully specified in the item description. Primary effort is structuring the parallel dispatch workflow and writing the report template format for SKILL.md.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:12321203a3d7e9ebf0222ed349ace9f3 -->\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGrep of `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/` and `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/*/skills/` for `shortlog`, `hotspot`, `bug magnet`, `bus factor`, `firefighting`, `momentum` returns zero matches \u2014 no local skill performs git-history-based risk identification. The `linear-walkthrough` skill traces execution paths through code but does not consume git metadata (file change frequency, fix commit clustering, contributor distribution). The `create-merge-request-changelog` skill consumes git history but only for the diff between two refs, not for whole-repo risk profiling.\\n\\nAs a result, when the orchestrator spawns code-review agents (e.g., `.claude/agents/code-review.md`, `code-reviewer` from various plugins), those agents have no signal indicating which files are highest-risk and should receive priority attention. The orchestrator cannot direct attention to \\\"this file changes the most AND has the most fix commits\\\" without manually constructing the git pipeline each time.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill at `./.claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md` is created. Its workflow:\\n\\n1. Probe repo size (commit count, contributor count) and select a calibrated time window \u2014 small repos analyze all history, medium 1 year, large 6 months\\n2. Run 7 git pipelines in parallel (orchestrator may dispatch individual Bash calls or use a single helper script):\\n   - hotspots: `git log --name-only --since=<window> | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -<N>`\\n   - bug magnets: `git log --grep='fix\\\\|bug\\\\|broken\\\\|hotfix\\\\|revert' --name-only --since=<window> | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -<N>`\\n   - bus factor: `git shortlog -sn --no-merges`\\n   - active vs total contributors (last 3 months)\\n   - momentum: `git log --since=<window> --format='%Y-%m' | sort | uniq -c`\\n   - firefighting: count of revert/hotfix/rollback commits in window\\n   - newly added files: `git log --since=<window> --diff-filter=A --name-only`\\n3. Cross-reference: intersect hotspots with bug magnets \u2192 high-risk file list with primary owner per file (`git shortlog -sn -- <file>`)\\n4. Output `walkthrough/recon-report.md` with 8 sections matching the codebase-recon report template\\n\\nThe skill is invocable as `/git-history-recon` and produces a markdown report consumable by `linear-walkthrough` (which can reference it during Phase 1 Discovery to prioritize coverage), `code-review` agents (which receive the high-risk file list as priority targets), and onboarding workflows.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`./.claude/skills/git-history-recon/SKILL.md` exists with frontmatter `name: git-history-recon`. Running `/git-history-recon` on a git repository writes `walkthrough/recon-report.md` containing literal section headers `## Code Hotspots`, `## Bug Magnets`, `## High-Risk Files`, `## Bus Factor`, `## Team Momentum`, `## Firefighting Frequency`, `## Recently Added Files`, `## Recommendations`. Each section contains at least one entry sourced from the corresponding git command. The High-Risk Files section is computed as the set intersection of hotspots and bug magnets, with each file annotated with its `git shortlog -sn -- <file>` primary owner. The skill validates with `uvx skilllint@latest check ./.claude/skills/git-history-recon/`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source Pattern\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nQuote from research entry section \\\"Key Features\\\" (lines 49-70): \\\"Seven-Dimension Parallel Analysis ... Code Hotspots: Most-changed files in the analysis window. Bus Factor: All-time contributor ranking by commit count. Bug Magnets: Files most associated with fix/bug/broken commits. ... Cross-Referencing and Risk Identification \u2014 High-Risk Files: Intersects code hotspots with bug magnets to identify files that are both frequently changed AND bug-prone. Risk Ownership: For each high-risk file, runs `git shortlog -sn -- <file>` to identify the primary owner.\\\"\\n\\nExternal tool: codebase-recon-skill (https://github.com/yujiachen-y/codebase-recon-skill)\\nInsights file: ./research/insights/2026-05-10-codebase-recon-skill-improvements.md (Improvement 2)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\